     "explanation": "Dirac predicted g = 2, but QED adds the effect of the electron's cloud of virtual particles, pushing g slightly higher. Schwinger's leading correction is a = alpha/(2 pi) = 0.0011614, and higher-order diagrams refine it further. Theory (0.00115965218 18...) and experiment (0.00115965218 07...) match to roughly twelve digits -- like measuring across the US to a hair's width. That precision, born from renormalization and the smallness of alpha, is why QED is called the most precisely tested theory in science.",
